  "noMusicReason": "Standing rule (2026-08-24 user directive): reels ship voice + SFX only, no music bed by default. Set plan[\"music\"] = true (or a full music object) to opt this reel back into a bed.",
  "format": "news",
  "script": "Your brand-new iPhone 18 Pro Max already had its battery drained once, before you ever touched it.\nThat's Prepare to Ship: a setting that exists on no other iPhone.\nHere's why: this phone's battery crossed a number no iPhone has ever crossed before, twenty watt-hours, all in one cell.\nSo every unit gets discharged at the factory, then capped, until it's activated.\nTurn it on, and the limit lifts, full battery, like you'd expect.\nCompare that to Apple's own 16-inch MacBook Pro, which holds even more power and never needs this.\nIt reportedly spreads the same total across several smaller cells, each one under that line.\nOne phone, one cell. That's the entire reason.\nShip this phone again, for repair, trade-in, resale, or as a gift, and it happens all over.\nThe battery discharges under that ceiling, running warm while it does.\nBut send it in for repair, trade-in, or return, and your charge gets capped at 80 percent for two weeks after.\nRemember that line: it shows up twice, once at the factory, once at your door.",
